Now WizardStore big edit. Need carefully rewrite imports and class. Let's plan diff.

Imports:
```
import { DestroyRef, Injectable, inject, isDevMode, signal, computed } from '@angular/core';
...
import type { ..., FormValue, InsurancePlan, PersistedWizardStateV1, QuotedPlan, WizardFormGroup, WizardStep } from '../../core/models';
import { calculateAdjustedPrice, formatCurrency, pickKeys } from '../../core/pricing/pricing.helper';
import { QuoteClock } from '../../core/pricing/quote-clock';
```

Private signals add:
```
private readonly plansSignal = signal<readonly InsurancePlan[]>([]);
private readonly plansStatusSignal = signal<CatalogueStatus>('idle');
private readonly plansErrorSignal = signal<string | null>(null);
private readonly invalidSelectionNoticeSignal = signal(false);
private readonly restoredSelectionNoticeSignal = signal(false);
private readonly restoredSelectionFromDraftSignal = signal(false);
private readonly quoteClockSignal = signal<QuoteClock | null>(null);

private readonly injectedClock = inject(QuoteClock);
```
Need order of `inject` fields before signals? All field initializers run in declaration order; injectedClock must be declared before used in computed. Put after factory etc.

Public:
```
readonly plans = this.plansSignal.asReadonly();
readonly plansStatus = ...;
readonly plansError = ...;
readonly invalidSelectionNotice = ...;
readonly restoredSelectionNotice = ...;
readonly step1Values = computed<Readonly<Record<string, FormValue>>>(() => {...});
readonly quotedPlans = computed<readonly QuotedPlan[]>(() => {...});
readonly selectedPlan = computed<InsurancePlan | null>(() => {...});
readonly canAdvance = computed<boolean>(() => ...);
```
Keep `selectedPlanDocumentId` existing alias. Need declaration order: step1Values needs formRevision, formSignal, fieldsSignal, factory; all declared. quotedPlans needs step1Values and plans etc. fine.

Methods:
```
captureClock(clock: QuoteClock): void { this.quoteClockSignal.set(clock); }

async loadPlans(country: CountryCode): Promise<void> { ... }
async retryPlans(): Promise<void> { await this.loadPlans(this.activeCountrySignal() ?? this.context.country()); }
selectPlan(documentId: string | null): void { ... }
```
But `retryPlans` returns Promise<void>; `async` with await fine. Could use `return this.loadPlans(...)`.
`loadPlans` catch: use try/catch with `await firstValueFrom`. Set plansStatus etc. Need careful with not clearing previous plans. Use `this.plansErrorSignal.set(this.describeError(error))`. `describeError` returns null in production; spec says dev-only HTTP detail; fine.
Success normalization:
```
const plans = await firstValueFrom(...);
this.plansSignal.set(plans);
const selected = this.selectedPlanSignal();
const restoredFromDraft = this.restoredSelectionFromDraftSignal();
if (selected !== null && plans.some(p => p.documentId === selected)) {
  this.invalidSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
  this.restoredSelectionNoticeSignal.set(restoredFromDraft);
} else if (selected !== null) {
  this.selectedPlanSignal.set(null);
  this.clearPersistedSelection(country);
  this.invalidSelectionNoticeSignal.set(true);
  this.restoredSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
} else {
  this.invalidSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
  this.restoredSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
}
this.plansStatusSignal.set(plans.length > 0 ? 'ready' : 'empty');
```
If plans empty and selected non-null, status empty plus invalid notice true; spec says empty state no false selection; notice maybe not shown because ready only. fine.
`selectPlan`:
```
if (documentId !== null && !this.plansSignal().some(p => p.documentId === documentId)) return;
this.selectedPlanSignal.set(documentId);
this.invalidSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
this.restoredSelectionNoticeSignal.set(false);
this.persist('plans');
```
For null: if called externally, persist null with updated savedAt; but we don't call it from loadPlans. Fine.

`clearPersistedSelection` uses persistence.load and save preserving savedAt but `load()` might discard if expired. Good.

`reset`: clear plans signals; notices false; quoteClockSignal null? Maybe keep? Reset should clear captured clock; set null. Add `restoredSelectionFromDraftSignal.set(false)`.
`startLoad`: at beginning after activeCountrySignal.set(country), clear Step2 signals:
