```
private readonly loadedCountry = signal<CountryCode | null>(null);
constructor() {
 effect(() => {
   const country = this.context.country();
   if (this.loadedCountry() !== country) {
     this.loadedCountry.set(country); // writing signal inside effect allowed? Angular effects can write signals, but with allowSignalWrites? In Angular 21 effects allow writes? To avoid issues, use untracked.
     untracked(() => { this.store.captureClock(this.clock); void this.store.loadPlans(country); });
   }
 });
 effect(() => {
   this.store.plansStatus();
   const heading = this.heading();
   if (heading) queueMicrotask(...)
 });
}
```
Writing signal in effect may throw NG0600 if signal writes disabled? Angular 19+ effects allow writes by default I think changed. To be safe use a plain field `private loadedCountry: CountryCode | null = null;` not reactive:
```
const country = this.context.country();
if (this.loadedCountry !== country) {
 this.loadedCountry = country;
 untracked(...)
}
```
Fine.
Focus effect reads `plansStatus()` and `heading()`; heading viewChild may be undefined on first run; after render, signal updates triggers effect again. Good.
Need `viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLElement>>('pageHeading')`.

Need import QuoteClock and store etc. `protected readonly store = inject(WizardStore); protected readonly context = inject(CountryContextService); private readonly router = inject(Router); private readonly clock = inject(QuoteClock);` In constructor `this.store.captureClock(this.clock)` before load.

