But `heading` viewChild might be undefined transiently while new branch not rendered; effect re-runs when query updates. fine.

Let's restructure template accordingly. Avoid duplicate `#pageHeading` across cases? Angular template compiler may complain about duplicate reference names in same template even in different @switch branches? Need test. Angular allows same template variable name in different embedded views? I think yes, e.g. `@if (a) { <input #ref> } @else { <input #ref> }` is common. Should compile.

